{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "An AsciiDoc processor is only required to provide limited support for validating internal cross references. Validation occurs when a cross reference is first visited. Since there are still some references aren’t stored in the parse tree (such as an anchor in the middle of a paragraph), which can lead to false positives, these validations are hidden behind a flag."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "When using Asciidoctor, you can enable validation of cross references in several ways:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "ulist",
        "id": null,
        "items": [
          {
            "blocks": [],
            "checkbox": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "when using the CLI, passing the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "-v"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " CLI option"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [],
            "checkbox": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "when using the API, setting the global variable "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "$VERBOSE"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to the value "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "true"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [],
            "checkbox": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "when using the API, setting the level on the global logger to INFO (i.e., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Asciidoctor::LoggerManager.logger.level = :info"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ")"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "style": null,
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "All of these adjustments put the processor into pedantic mode. In this mode, the parser will immediately validate cross references, issuing a warning message if the reference is not valid. If you set the global variable "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "$VERBOSE"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " to "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "true"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", it will also enable warnings in Ruby, which may not be what you want."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Consider the following example:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "See <<foobar>>.\n\n[#foobaz]\n== Foobaz"
          }
        ],
        "language": "asciidoc",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "If you run Asciidoctor in verbose/pedantic mode on this document ("
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "-v"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "), it will send the following warning message to the logger."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "literal",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "asciidoctor: WARNING: invalid reference: foobar"
          }
        ],
        "language": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "An AsciiDoc processor is only required to validate references within the same document (after any includes are resolved)."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Validate Cross References"
      }
    ]
  }
}
